v></div></div><div role=\"listitem\" class=\"process-step-item w-dyn-item\"><div class=\"process-step-header\"><div class=\"tab-circle\"><div class=\"step-number\">4</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"line-bar\"></div></div><div class=\"process-content-wrapper w-dyn-list\"><div role=\"list\" class=\"process-content-list w-dyn-items\"><div role=\"listitem\" class=\"process-content-item w-dyn-item\"><div class=\"process-step\"><div class=\"image-step-tab\"><img alt=\"Technician inspecting an old tiled spa with a broken brick coping before a pool remodel in Florida\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-064/pool-remodeling-assessment-old-spa-inspection.avif\" class=\"img-process\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\"></div><div class=\"content-step-tab\"><div class=\"wrapper-vertical-text\"><h2>Pool Assessment &amp; Condition Analysis</h2><div class=\"text-divider\"><div class=\"w-richtext\"><p>Detailed inspection identifying plaster delamination, structural cracks, equipment aging, circulation inefficiencies, and aesthetic improvements needed. We use underwater camera inspection to assess interior conditions and plan targeted renovations.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div role=\"listitem\" class=\"process-content-item w-dyn-item\"><div class=\"process-step\"><div class=\"image-step-tab\"><img alt=\"French-pattern travertine deck and cobalt tile around a raised spa, materials for a pool renovation in Florida\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-053/pool-renovation-travertine-deck-cobalt-tile-spa.avif\" class=\"img-process\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1200\"></div><div class=\"content-step-tab\"><div class=\"wrapper-vertical-text\"><h2>Renovation Design &amp; Material Selection</h2><div class=\"text-divider\"><div class=\"w-richtext\"><p>Design consultation for modernization including updated finishes, enhanced circulation systems, lighting upgrades, and deck resurfacing options. We present 3D renderings showing before/after transformations.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div role=\"listitem\" class=\"process-content-item w-dyn-item\"><div class=\"process-step\"><div class=\"image-step-tab\"><img alt=\"Crew cutting block and setting the deck around a drained pool during a pool remodeling project in Florida\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-048/pool-remodeling-crew-at-work-on-drained-pool.avif\" class=\"img-process\" width=\"1260\" height=\"840\" style=\"object-position:15% 50%\"></div><div class=\"content-step-tab\"><div class=\"wrapper-vertical-text\"><h2>Permits &amp; Project Coordination</h2><div class=\"text-divider\"><div class=\"w-richtext\"><p>Acquisition of renovation permits and coordinated scheduling with utility providers. For major renovations, Notice of Commencement filing and ARB re-approval may be required.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div role=\"listitem\" class=\"process-content-item w-dyn-item\"><div class=\"process-step\"><div class=\"image-step-tab\"><img alt=\"Two workers hand-troweling new white plaster in a drained pool with blue waterline tile, pool renovation in Florida\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/obra/obra-064/pool-renovation-new-white-plaster-hand-troweled.avif\" class=\"img-process\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" style=\"object-position:35% 50%\"></div><div class=\"content-step-tab\"><div class=\"wrapper-vertical-text\"><h2>Renovation Execution &amp; System Upgrades</h2><div class=\"text-divider\"><div class=\"w-richtext\"><p>Full renovation including surface restoration, equipment replacement, circulation upgrades, and integration of smart automation systems for enhanced functionality and energy efficiency.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"w-embed w-script\"><script>\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {\n\n  const AUTOPLAY_DELAY = 5000;\n\n  const COLOR_ACTIVE   = '#001C63';\n  const COLOR_INACTIVE = '#D99933';\n\n  const dots  = document.querySelectorAll('.process-step-item');\n  const steps = document.querySelectorAll('.process-content-item');\n\n  if (!dots.length || !steps.length) return;\n\n  let currentStep = 0;\n  let autoTimer   = null;\n  let isAnimating = false;\n\n  function goToStep(index) {\n    if (isAnimating) return;\n    isAnimating = true;\n\n    const prevStep = currentStep;\n    currentStep = index;\n\n    // ── 1. Actualizar DOTS (nav) ──────────────────────────\n    dots.forEach(function (dot, i) {\n      const circle = dot.querySelector('.tab-circle, [class*=\"tab-circle\"], [class*=\"Tab-Circle\"]');\n      const number = dot.querySelector('[class*=\"step-number\"], [class*=\"Step-Number\"]'); // ✅ DENTRO de goToStep\n\n      if (!circle) return;\n\n      if (i === currentStep) {\n        circle.style.background = COLOR_ACTIVE;\n        circle.style.transform  = 'scale(1.15)';\n        circle.style.boxShadow  = '0 4px 16px rgba(0,28,99,0.25)';\n        circle.style.transition = 'all 0.35s ease';\n        if (number) number.style.color = '#FFFFFF'; // ✅ Blanco activo\n      } else {\n        circle.style.background = COLOR_INACTIVE;\n        circle.style.transform  = 'scale(1)';\n        circle.style.boxShadow  = 'none';\n        circle.style.transition = 'all 0.35s ease';\n        if (number) number.style.color = '#001C63'; // ✅ Navy inactivo\n      }\n    });\n\n    // ── 2. Animar salida del paso anterior ────────────────\n    if (steps[prevStep] && prevStep !== currentStep) {\n      const outEl = steps[prevStep];\n      outEl.style.transition = 'opacity 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease';\n      outEl.style.opacity    = '0';\n      outEl.style.transform  = 'translateY(-10px)';\n\n      setTimeout(function () {\n        outEl.style.display = 'none';\n        showCurrentStep();\n      }, 300);\n    } else {\n      showCurrentStep();\n    }\n  }\n\n  function showCurrentStep() {\n    steps.forEach(function (s) {\n      s.style.display = 'none';\n      s.style.opacity = '0';\n    });\n\n    const activeEl = steps[currentStep];\n    if (!activeEl) { isAnimating = false; return; }\n\n    activeEl.style.display   = 'flex';\n    activeEl.style.transform = 'translateY(12px)';\n    activeEl.style.opacity   = '0';\n\n    void activeEl.offsetWidth;\n\n    activeEl.style.transition = 'opacity 0.4s ease, transform 0.4s ease';\n    activeEl.style.opacity    = '1';\n    activeEl.style.transform  = 'translateY(0)';\n\n    setTimeout(function () { isAnimating = false; }, 420);\n  }\n\n  function startAutoplay() {\n    stopAutoplay();\n    autoTimer = setInterval(function () {\n      const next = (currentStep + 1) % dots.length;\n      goToStep(next);\n    }, AUTOPLAY_DELAY);\n  }\n\n  function stopAutoplay() {\n    if (autoTimer) { clearInterval(autoTimer); autoTimer = null; }\n  }\n\n  dots.forEach(function (dot, i) {\n    dot.style.cursor = 'pointer';\n    dot.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      if (i === currentStep) return;\n      stopAutoplay();\n      goToStep(i);\n      startAutoplay();\n    });\n  });\n\n  const section = document.querySelector('.process-section');\n  if (section) {\n    section.addEventListener('mouseenter', stopAutoplay);\n    section.addEventListener('mouseleave', startAutoplay);\n  }\n\n  goToStep(0);\n  startAutoplay();\n\n});\n</script></div></div><img sizes=\"100vw\" srcset=\"/images/site/design3-p-500.webp 500w, /images/site/design3-p-800.webp 800w, /images/site/design3-p-1080.webp 1080w, /images/site/design3-p-1600.webp 1600w, /images/site/design3.webp 1920w\" alt=\"\" src=\"/images/site/design3.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"design-bg\" width=\"1920\" height=\"255\"></section>";
const T6 = "<section class=\"faq-section\"><div class=\"w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container\"><div data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bc3\" class=\"header-faq\"><h2>Pool Remodeling FAQs</h2><div>Have questions about pool remodeling in Florida? Our licensed pool contractors answer the top questions from North and South Florida homeowners below.</div></div><div class=\"wrapper-faq-components\"><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bc7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Why remodel a pool in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Pool remodeling improves efficiency, safety, appearance, and long-term property value, making Florida pools significantly easier to enjoy. Licensed under CPC1460562 and CPC1461119, Mr. &amp; Mrs. Outdoor Living handles the full scope — from structural inspection through final finish application.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bcf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">What energy savings can pool upgrades provide?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">It depends on the equipment being replaced and how the pool is run, so we do not quote a percentage. Variable-speed pumps are the biggest lever: they move the same water at lower speeds for most of the day, and Florida law (section 553.909, Florida Statutes) already requires residential pool pumps of 1 horsepower or more to run at two or more speeds. In a complete remodel we size the pump, filtration and low-voltage LED lighting to the renovated pool as one system, instead of swapping parts one at a time.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bd7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">How long does a pool remodel take in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">It depends on the scope: an interior refinish with new tile moves faster than a remodel that rebuilds the shell, replaces the equipment and redoes the deck. We assess the pool first and give you the schedule for your scope in writing, together with the fixed project price, before any demolition starts. Permit review and inspections are part of that schedule, and we coordinate them.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bdf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Can features be added during a pool renovation?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. Pool renovations are an ideal time to add spas, tanning ledges, waterfalls, LED lighting, and smart automation systems. Our licensed pool contractors manage the permitting and installation of all additions alongside the renovation work, keeping your project coordinated and on schedule.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077be7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Do you offer financing options for outdoor projects?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. We connect Florida homeowners with lending partners, and the order matters: you get the scope of the renovation and a fixed project price in writing first, and only then review how to pay for it. Approval and terms come from the lender.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">How much does a complete pool remodel cost in North Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">There is no single number: a remodel is priced from the condition of the shell, the finish and tile you choose, the equipment being replaced and the deck work around it. Our estimator walks you through those choices, and you get a fixed project price in writing before any demolition starts.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Does a pool remodel need a permit in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Usually, yes. Work that touches the structure, plumbing, electrical, equipment or the safety barrier is permitted and inspected under the Florida Building Code; resurfacing alone is treated differently by different jurisdictions. We confirm the scope with the building department and pull the permits under our license.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\" width=\"12\" height=\"7\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">What is included in a complete pool remodel?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">An assessment of the shell and plumbing, then the scope you choose: interior finish, waterline tile and coping, equipment and lighting, a spa added or rebuilt, deck resurfacing or replacement, and a code-compliant barrier, finished with start-up and a walk-through of the new equipment.</p></nav></div></div></div><img sizes=\"100vw\" srcset=\"/images/site/design2-p-500.webp 500w, /images/site/design2-p-800.webp 800w, /images/site/design2-p-1080.webp 1080w, /images/site/design2-p-1600.webp 1600w, /images/site/design2.webp 1920w\" alt=\"\" src=\"/images/site/design2.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"design-bg\" width=\"1920\" height=\"146\"></section><section class=\"testimonial-section\"><div class=\"w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container\"><div data-w-id=\"74852c7c-aeb3-35a7-5cf1-44f4ce6ecae5\" class=\"header-reviews\"><div class=\"label\">TESTIMONIALS</div><h2 class=\"white\">What Our Clients Say About Mr &amp; Mrs Outdoor Living</h2><p>Read testimonials from Florida clients enjoying safer, more beautiful pools after professional renovation by our licensed pool remodeling contractors.</p></div>";
